Receiving SNMP traps in OMD sites
=================================

Every site with SNMPTRAPD=on runs its own snmptrapd on a site-specific
UDP port. A central component receives the traps on UDP/162 and copies
them to all these sites. There are two methods for the central
component. Install EITHER method A OR method B, never both (both want
to own UDP/162).

A) samplicate (available on all distributions)
B) snmptrapd mirror (only available if the directory
   /opt/omd/versions/default/share/snmptrapd_mirror exists. It requires
   a net-snmp version which knows addForwarderInfo, i.e. 5.9 or newer.)


0) prerequisite (as root, both methods)
   The site snmptrapd is the one from the distribution: /usr/sbin/snmptrapd
   Debian/Ubuntu:   apt-get install snmptrapd
   RHEL family:     dnf install net-snmp    (usually already installed with OMD)
   SLES/openSUSE:   zypper install net-snmp (usually already installed with OMD)


1) as site-user (in every site which shall receive traps)
omd config set SNMPTRAPD on
omd start snmptrapd


2A) samplicate, as root
/bin/cp /opt/omd/versions/default/share/samplicate/*.service /etc/systemd/system
systemctl stop snmptrapd.socket snmptrapd 2>/dev/null
systemctl disable snmptrapd.socket snmptrapd 2>/dev/null
systemctl enable samplicate
systemctl enable samplicate_watch
systemctl restart samplicate_watch

   Rollback:
systemctl stop samplicate_watch samplicate
systemctl disable samplicate_watch samplicate
rm /etc/systemd/system/samplicate_watch.service /etc/systemd/system/samplicate.service
systemctl daemon-reload


2B) snmptrapd mirror, as root
   The mirror is the distribution's snmptrapd.service. A drop-in gives it
   the same command line on all distributions (without a -L logging
   destination, so the journal does not get one entry per trap).
   On Debian/Ubuntu, snmptrapd.socket must stay enabled (package default).
/bin/cp /opt/omd/versions/default/share/snmptrapd_mirror/snmptrapd_mirror_watch.service /etc/systemd/system
mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/snmptrapd.service.d
/bin/cp /opt/omd/versions/default/share/snmptrapd_mirror/omd-mirror.conf /etc/systemd/system/snmptrapd.service.d
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable snmptrapd_mirror_watch
systemctl start snmptrapd_mirror_watch
   # the watcher writes the managed section of /etc/snmp/snmptrapd.conf
   # and starts/reloads/stops snmptrapd.service within ~60s. Do not enable
   # snmptrapd.service yourself.
   # Details: /opt/omd/versions/default/share/snmptrapd_mirror/README.snmptrapd

   Rollback:
systemctl stop snmptrapd_mirror_watch snmptrapd
systemctl disable snmptrapd_mirror_watch
rm /etc/systemd/system/snmptrapd_mirror_watch.service
rm /etc/systemd/system/snmptrapd.service.d/omd-mirror.conf
systemctl daemon-reload
rm /etc/snmp/snmptrapd.conf
